      "text": "**Project Hail Mary** is a science fiction novel by Andy Weir, published in 2021. The story follows Ryland Grace, a middle-school science teacher who wakes up alone on a spacecraft and gradually recalls his mission: to investigate a microorganism called Astrophage that is threatening to dim the sun and endanger life on Earth. Alongside an alien named Rocky, Grace works to solve this existential crisis while navigating the challenges of deep space.\n\n### Key Information:\n- **Publication Year**: 2021\n- **Reception**: The novel received high praise for its scientific rigor, optimistic tone, and character development. It has garnered an average rating of 4.8/5 from over 47,000 readers on various platforms.\n- **Themes**: Major themes include science and problem-solving, first contact, sacrifice, friendship, and survival.\n\n### Awards and Recognition:\nWhile specific awards weren't mentioned in the search results, the novel has been recognized as one of the best science fiction novels of 2021 by multiple publications.\n\nFor more in-depth information, you can refer to its [Wikipedia page](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Hail_Mary), which offers additional insights into the plot and its significance in contemporary science fiction literature.",
